					type: "header",
					title: "Dinosaur Land",
					tagline: "A Jurassic Paradise",
					image: "header.png",
				},		
				{
					type: "appeared-table",
					firstAppeared: {
						game: "Super Mario World",
						year: 2001,
						link: "https://www.mariowiki.com/Super_Mario_World:_Super_Mario_Advance_2"
					},
					lastAppeared: {
						game: "Super Mario RPG",
						year: 2023,
						link: "https://www.mariowiki.com/Super_Mario_RPG_(Nintendo_Switch)"
					}
				},
				{
					type: "text",
					content: "Off the coast of the Cascade Kingdom is the small archipelago of dino-filled isles that make up Dinosaur Land! While most know for Yoshi's Island, there are many locations to be found along these lively shores. Here you will find a host of creatures including Blarggs, dino-Rhinos, Dino-Torches, Eeries, Rexes and Reznors as well as Dolphins, Swoopers - and you can't forget Yoshis!",
					alignContent: "left",
				},
				{
					type: "image",
					alignImage: "center",
					image: "dinosaur_land.webp",
					caption: "Dinosaur Land Map",
					alignCaption: "center",
				},
				{
					type: "text",
					title: "Mainland",
					titleColor: "#b18f01",
					content: "The central part of the archipelago consists of 6 main landmasses circling the Valley of Bowser. Connecting to Yoshi's Island is Donut Plains, bubbly grasslands perfect to go-kart in. From there you may stumble into the the Vanilla Dome caves, or go along the Twin Bridges to Cookie Mountain. Don't get lost in the Forest of Illusion - and do NOT eat the rocks on Chocolate Island.",
					alignContent: "left",
				},
				{
					type: "carousel",
					images: [
						{
							image: "donut_plains.png",
							caption: "Donut Plains"
						},
						{
							image: "vanilla_dome.png",
							caption: "Vanilla Dome"
						},
						{
							image: "twin_bridges.png",
							caption: "Twin Bridges"
						},
						{
							image: "forest_of_illusion.png",
							caption: "Forest of Illusion"
						},
						{
							image: "chocolate_island.png",
							caption: "Chocolate Island"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					type: "image-right",
					image: "choco_mountain.webp",
					caption: "Choco Mountain",
					content: "After Mario's visit in Super Mario World, he and his friends returned often for Go-Karting, Tennis, and a multitude of other sports! You will find many race tracks and battle courses set here. Keep an eye out for the swirly hills of Donut Plains, and the rocky cliffs of Choco Mountain."
				},
				{
					type: "image",
					alignImage: "center",
					image: "donut_plains.webp",
					caption: "Donut Plains 3",
					alignCaption: "center",
				},
			],

			right: [
				{
					type: "text",
					title: "Yoshi's Island",
					titleColor: "#b18f01",
					content: "Where Yoshi was first discovered, and first aided the Mario Bros. home, it is full of vast and varied biomes. There are grassy hills, mountainous peaks, primaeval jungles, icy cliffs, gorgeous beaches and arid badlands. Giant fruit and flora cover the isle, with the Super Happy Tree as the source of their food and happiness. The isle has taken many forms in its history, but none will deny the comfort that it brings.",
					alignContent: "left",
				},
				{
					type: "carousel",
					images: [
						{
							image: "yoshi_gif.gif",
							caption: "Yoshi's Island from the Original"
						},
						{
							image: "yoshi_ds.png",
							caption: "Yoshi's Island from the DS"
						},
						{
							image: "yoshi_rpg.png",
