						link: "https://www.mariowiki.com/Paper_Mario:_The_Thousand-Year_Door_(Nintendo_Switch)"
					}
				},
				{
					type: "text",
					content: "The shady run-down port town that hides more than just a criminal underworld. After the battle between the Four Heroes and the Shadow Queen, the people built Rogueport over the old city and the Thousand-Year Door. The port town now is a hub of danger in the Mushroom Kingdom; with the Robbos lurking about the East, and the Pianta Syndicate controlling the West - entering a back alley may result in a robbery or worse.",
					alignContent: "left",
				},
				{
					type: "image",
					alignImage: "center",
					image: "plaza.jpg",
					caption: "Rogueport Plaza",
					alignCaption: "center",
				},
				{
					type: "text",
					content: "Rogueport connects to many interesting locals nearby, many of them accessible from Rogueport Station. You can hop aboard intercity trains or blimps here!",
					alignContent: "left",
